From: monoflow-ayvu <dev@ayvu>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 14:45:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: never power-collapse the VPU on no-TZ systems

QCS6490 quirk: booted via the no-TZ path (KODIAKWP firmware), the VPU
firmware does not reliably report WFI/idle at session teardown, so the
idle poll in venus_suspend_3xx() intermittently fails (-ETIMEDOUT;
"wait for cpu and video core idle fail (-110)", after which every later
session fails until reboot). Hardware validation on the Dragon Q6A
further showed that a collapse done without the firmware's
prepare-power-collapse handshake leaves the core unbootable on the next
resume ("failed to reset venus core" in venus_boot_core()).

Never power-collapse on no-TZ systems: venus_runtime_suspend() becomes
a no-op, the VPU stays powered across sessions, and both failure modes
become unreachable. Power saving is explicitly not required on this
platform. The resume path is unaffected: venus_power_on() is a no-op
while hdev->power_enabled is set.

Signed-off-by: monoflow-ayvu <dev@ayvu>
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
index abf959b..8129bfc 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/core.c
@@ -580,6 +580,19 @@ static __maybe_unused int venus_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	const struct venus_pm_ops *pm_ops = core->pm_ops;
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * QCS6490 quirk: booted via the no-TZ path (KODIAKWP firmware),
+	 * the VPU firmware does not reliably report WFI/idle at session
+	 * teardown, so the idle poll in venus_suspend_3xx() intermittently
+	 * fails (-ETIMEDOUT), and a collapse done without the firmware's
+	 * prepare handshake leaves the core unbootable on the next resume
+	 * ("failed to reset venus core"). Never power-collapse on no-TZ
+	 * systems; power saving is not required. The resume path is
+	 * unaffected: venus_power_on() is a no-op while power_enabled.
+	 */
+	if (!core->use_tz)
+		return 0;
+
 	ret = hfi_core_suspend(core);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
-- 
2.51.0
